<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">West Pakistan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1955">1955</a>–<a href="/years/1970">1970</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">West <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> was the single province formed in 1955 under the One Unit scheme by merging the provinces and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> of the western wing of Pakistan, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/punjab">Punjab</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a>, the North-West Frontier, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/balochistan">Baluchistan</a>, Bahawalpur, Khairpur and the Baluchistan States Union. The princely states lost their separate status. It was dissolved in 1970 and the old provinces were restored.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/west-pakistan.jpg" alt="West Pakistan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: EnchantedEdits · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:West_Pakistan_(orthographic_projection).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
